* Stuck swarm bees (openc2e Creatures 2 project, our own script). Run by
* openc2e after the world loads (Additions folder); made anew each load.
*
* When a hive (2 16 2) dies out it sends out a queen (2 17 5) and 20 swarm
* bees (2 17 6) that follow her; once she has built a new hive they fly to it
* (OV00 1, OV01 the hive) and join it on arrival (its OV10 up 5, the bee gone).
* Swarm bees bump into walls and floors, and nothing in the game's scripts
* frees one that is pinned: in Home (owner, 2026-11-21: "fix these bees being
* stuck here? they've been there for a while") fifteen hung still, three in
* the sea under the west dock trying to fly up through it, four stacked
* against the rock at 6610,1905, others in caves, their queen long gone.
*
* A watcher (2 1 165, every 100 ticks) looks at each swarm bee: one that has
* not moved more than 2 px in four looks (about 40 seconds) joins its hive
* as it would on arriving (OV01 a hive still there: its OV10 up 5), and goes.
* A pinned one with no hive left just goes. OV60-OV62 are the watcher's
* (last place, looks without moving); the game's bee scripts use OV00-OV11.
enum 2 1 165 kill targ next
inst new: simp blnk 1 0 0 0 setv cls2 2 1 165 setv attr 16 mvto 5000 1350 tick 100 slow
scrp 2 1 165 9
  inst
  enum 2 17 6
    setv var1 posl subv var1 ov60
    setv var2 post subv var2 ov61
    setv var0 0
    doif var1 le 2 and var1 ge -2 and var2 le 2 and var2 ge -2 setv var0 1 endi
    doif var0 eq 1
      addv ov62 1
    else
      setv ov62 0
    endi
    setv ov60 posl setv ov61 post
    doif ov62 ge 4
      setv var3 targ
      setv var4 0
      doif ov00 eq 1 setv var4 ov01 endi
      enum 2 16 2
        doif targ eq var4 addv ov10 5 endi
      next
      targ var3
      kill targ
    endi
  next
endm
